Subject: safe mode: the boot members the owner marked safe=1 load too

Safe mode loaded no boot-class module, so a box whose only NIC is a
module (every Z3660 box) had no network in a safe boot.  A boot record
with safe=1 (kbootset writes it from a `safe` line in modreg.local.d,
S5-09, C4-4 section 2) now loads in safe mode as well: marc_post's boot
pass takes only those, the demand pass is skipped, and lf_gate lets
only those through.  Without such a record the old line and behaviour
stand.  The state harness has the marked and unmarked members.

